    "filed_by": "outer-loop (Claude Sonnet 5), user authorized starting ARC-specific outer-loop work",
    "root_cause": "This artifact's own recorded training_shard_count=3/training_example_count=10000 confirms the original 2026-06-20 run only ever staged the '10k truncated mirror' (per the original manifest's own 'staged' note). A later, undocumented partial restaging attempt produced 4 shards / 14,797 examples on disk -- still far short of the full 340-session raw corpus -- and every row's level_progress read 0.0 (verified directly: a full 1564-step winning session showed level_progress=0.0 start to finish). The conversion CODE (python/carnot/agentic/arc_human_replay_corpus.py) was verified correct by direct testing against the raw parquet mirror; the bug was that the staged output on disk was simply stale/incomplete, never regenerated with the full raw corpus.",
    "fix": "Re-ran corpus.write_training_shards_from_parquet() against all 7 raw HF mirror parquet files (already downloaded, no network re-fetch needed) with the existing, unmodified conversion code. No code changes were needed -- only the missing full regeneration.",
    "corrected_shard_state": {
      "training_shard_count": 44,
